ˇCçe¯[^âÏ]√Try `%s --help' for more information.
␀Usage: %s [OPTION]... [INPUT [OUTPUT]]
␀
  -c, --count           prefix lines by the number of occurrences
  -d, --repeated        only print duplicate lines
  -f, --skip-fields=N   avoid comparing the N first fields
  -s, --skip-chars=N    avoid comparing the N first characters
  -u, --unique          only print unique lines
  -w, --check-chars=N   compare no more then N characters in lines
  -N                    same as -f N
  +N                    same as -s N
      --help            display this help and exit
      --version         output version information and exit

A field is a run of whitespace, than non whitespace characters.
Fields are skipped before chars.  If OUTPUT not specified, writes to
standard output.  If INPUT not specified, reads from standard input.
