␀Usage: %s [OPTION] [PATH]...
␀
  -a, --all                 include filesystems having 0 blocks
  -i, --inodes              list inode information instead of block usage
  -k, --kilobytes           use 1024 blocks, not 512 despite POSIXLY_CORRECT
      --sync                invoke sync before getting usage info (default)
      --no-sync             do not invoke sync before getting usage info
  -t, --type=TYPE           limit the listing to TYPE filesystems type
  -x, --exclude-type=TYPE   limit the listing to not TYPE filesystems type
  -v                        (ignored)
  -P, --portability         use the POSIX output format
  -T, --print-type          print filesystem type
      --help                display this help and exit
      --version             output version information and exit

If no PATHs are given, list all currently mounted filesystems.
