><DIV
CLASS="SECTION"
><H1
CLASS="SECTION"
><A
NAME="CONFIGURE-SCRIPTING"
>2.4. Configure Scripting</A
></H1
><P
>Like many other open source projects, Bochs uses a configure script created with
<B
CLASS="COMMAND"
>autoconf</B
>. The configure script generates all makefiles and a
set of header and support files from templates.</P
><P
>This example shows how to add an option to the template file <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>configure.in</TT
>.
The resulting configure script sets up symbols like <CODE
CLASS="OPTION"
>BX_SUPPORT_BUSMOUSE</CODE
>
in the output file <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>config.h</TT
> and replaces <CODE
CLASS="OPTION"
>@BUSM_OBJS@</CODE
>
entries in the makefile output.
<PRE
CLASS="SCREEN"
>BUSM_OBJS=''
AC_MSG_CHECKING(for Busmouse support)
AC_ARG_ENABLE(busmouse,
  AS_HELP_STRING([--enable-busmouse], [enable Busmouse support (InPort)]),
  [if test "$enableval" = yes; then
    AC_MSG_RESULT(yes)
    AC_DEFINE(BX_SUPPORT_BUSMOUSE, 1)
    BUSM_OBJS='busmouse.o'
   else
    AC_MSG_RESULT(no)
    AC_DEFINE(BX_SUPPORT_BUSMOUSE, 0)
   fi],
  [
    AC_DEFINE(BX_SUPPORT_BUSMOUSE, 0)
    AC_MSG_RESULT(no)]
  )
AC_SUBST(BUSM_OBJS)</PRE
></P
><P
>These output files are generated by the configure script in addition to the makefiles.
<P
></P
><UL
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>config.h</TT
> - the main header file</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>ltdlconf.h</TT
> - header file required for compiling with libtool</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>bxversion.h</TT
> - header file containing version strings</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>bxversion.rc</TT
> - resource file for Windows with version information</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>build/linux/bochs-dlx</TT
> - DLX Linux shortcut script (Linux only)</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>build/macosx/Info.plist</TT
> - property list file for MacOSX</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>build/win32/nsis/bochs.nsi</TT
> - NSIS script for creating Windows installer package</P
></LI
></UL
></P
></DIV
