><DIV
CLASS="SECTION"
><H1
CLASS="SECTION"
><A
NAME="SEARCH-ORDER"
>5.2. Search order for the configuration file</A
></H1
><P
>If no configuration file is specified on the command line and config file loading
is not disabled, Bochs searches for a default configuration file. This is the search order:
<P
></P
><OL
TYPE="1"
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>.bochsrc</TT
> in the current directory</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>bochsrc</TT
> in the current directory</P
></LI
><LI
><P
><TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>bochsrc.txt</TT
> in the current directory</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>(win32 only) <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>bochsrc.bxrc</TT
> in the current directory</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>(Unix only) <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>.bochsrc</TT
> in the user's home directory</P
></LI
><LI
><P
>(Unix only) <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>bochsrc</TT
> in the <TT
CLASS="FILENAME"
>/etc</TT
> directory</P
></LI
></OL
></P
></DIV
