␀SB16 emulator control program for Bochs.

Usage: sb16ctrl [-i #] [-t #,#,#,#,#,#] [-r] [-m #,..] [-f filename]

This program is used to control the operation of the SB16 emulator
until it has a more sophisticated interface.
Any number of commands can be given. If none are present "-f -"
is assumed.

-i # show the selected emulator info string
-t #,#,#,#,#,# load the patch translation into the emulator
-r resets the patch translation table
-m #,... sends the given midi message (up to 255 bytes)
-f filename loads commands from the given file, or stdin if "-"
-v be verbose

# can be decimal, octal (first digit 0) or hexadecimal (0x..)

SB16CTRL is Copyright (C) 1999 by Josef Drexler.
