í␀␀ÉƒÉÏ°†oG␀ˇpTËë␀␀ÉƒÈ≈␀␀␀ÉÏhcÿ@␀°∞kG␀çÖ␀␀␀␀°pmG␀ˇ4Ë∏•␀ÉƒâEÙÉ}Ù␀Ñî␀␀␀ÉÏçEÏPçEPˇuÙË¥␀ÉƒÉÏçE»PˇuÙË¨¥␀ÉƒÉÏçE»PˇuÏˇu°∞kG␀çÖ␀␀␀␀°pmG␀ˇ4hfÿ@␀h∞oG␀ËZ>␀Éƒ ÉÏh∞oG␀°†oG␀ˇpTËNë␀␀ÉƒÉÏ°†oG␀ˇpTË^ê␀␀ÉƒÉÏˇuÙË?␀ÉƒÉÏj°∞kG␀çÖ␀␀␀␀°pmG␀ˇ4Ë=˘ˇˇÉƒ…√##␀êç¥&␀␀␀␀This is the list of available themes. Choose any theme and click 'Apply' to select it␀UâÂÉÏÉÏhˇ␀␀␀hÄmG␀°‡lG␀çÖ␀␀␀␀°ê!E␀ˇ4Ëq≤␀␀ÉƒÉÏh’⁄@␀hÄmG␀Ëô=␀ÉƒÉÏh‡⁄@␀hÄmG␀ËÑ=␀ÉƒÉÏhÄmG␀°`mG␀ˇpTË8ê␀␀ÉƒÉÏ°`mG␀ˇpTËHè␀␀Éƒ…√çt&␀{ÆG·zÑ?UâÂ€xlG␀›¿€@␀ﬁ…›ÄlG␀]√UâÂ°∏kG␀çÖ␀␀␀␀°¸ E␀ã£!E␀]√ê␀␀zDUâÂ€†lG␀Ÿ␀‹@␀ﬁ˘Ÿ§lG␀]√No Limit␀100 FPS␀Off␀Low␀Medium␀High␀Kids␀Easy␀Hard␀Menu␀Graphics␀Local Game␀Controls␀Advanced Options␀Audio␀Editor␀Delete Set␀Select Theme␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêA local game with up to 4 alternating players.␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêA two-player or deathmatch game via Internet or LAN.␀Network Game␀Quick Help␀␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêThere's nasty work out there waiting for you... better stay here!␀Quit␀On␀Sound:␀Speech:␀Volume:␀Back␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêIf you turn animations low there'll be less details which will speed up the game a great deal.␀Animations:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêIf this is enabled you'll see the time left for all bonuses and maluses at the right side of the screen.␀Bonus Info:␀Fullscreen␀Window␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêYou may run LBreakout2 either fullscreen or windowed. This switch may be done anywhere by pressing 'f'.␀Display:␀ÎêêêêêêêêêêêêêYou you don't want LBreakout2 to consume all of your CPU (best performance) limit the frame rate.␀Frame Rate:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêIn this menu you can change the appearance of LBreakout. Included to the release are the three winning themes from the Linux Game Tome contest 'absoluteB','Oz' and 'Moiree' along with the old graphics as theme 'Classic'.#For more themes check out http://lgames.sf.net.␀???␀Resume Last Game␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêPlay the original LBreakout2 levelset.␀Start Original Set␀ç∂␀␀␀␀Play the additional levelset selected below.␀Start AddOn␀AddOn:␀KIDS:#Lives: 9 (max. 12)#Paddle Size: 252 (max. 396)#Ball Speed: 100-200#Bonus: -50% (no maluses, no bad speech)##EASY:#Lives: 6 (max. 9)#Paddle Size: 72 (max. 180)#Ball Speed: 240-400 pixels/sec#Bonus: -20%##MEDIUM:#Lives: 5 (max. 7)#Paddle Size: 54 (max. 144)#Ball Speed: 270-430 pixels/sec##HARD:#Lives: 4 (max. 5)#Paddle Size: 54 (max. 108)#Ball Speed: 300-450 pixels/sec#Bonus: +30%␀Difficulty:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêThese are the number of players and their names. If one player looses a ball or restarts the level it's the next player's turn.␀Players:␀1st:␀2nd:␀3rd:␀4th:␀çv␀If you use the keyboard for input these are the keys for moving the paddle ('Paddle Turbo' will double the speed while pressed.), firing balls/shots and returning the ball to paddle after a timeout of ten seconds.##Note: If balls are fired at a random angle (which has become the default) there is no difference between the left or right fire key. A sticky paddle stops a ball until any fire button is pressed but the movement angle is the one from the normal reflection. To reset the movement angle to -50 or +50 degrees check out 'Ball Fire Angle' in 'Advanced Options'.##While pressed, the 'Ball Turbo' will bring all balls to the maximum speed defined in 'Advanced Options'.␀Left:␀Right:␀Left Fire:␀Right Fire:␀Paddle Turbo:␀Ball Turbo:␀Return:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêAdjust the paddle speed for movement by keys. (pixels per second)␀Key Speed:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêThis modifies the relative motion of the mouse. (percent) The higher this value is the faster the mouse moves.␀Motion Modifier:␀If for some reason your mouse movement is inverted you can fix it with this option.␀Invert Motion:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêAs long as this option is enabled the paddle is treated as convex allowing easy aiming. If you disable this option the real physics will show up and you'll have to influence the ball by paddle movement and the hemispherical ends. Just for cracks.␀Convex Paddle:␀Random␀50␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêIf '50' the ball is shot at an angle of 50 degrees to the left or right, depending on which fire button has been pressed. If it is set to 'random' the ball is fired at a random angle. In this case a sticky paddle simply halts the normal reflection until any fire button has been pressed.␀Ball Fire Angle:␀Above Bonuses␀Below Bonuses␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêIf you can't see the ball because of thousands of bonuses coming down set this option to 'Above Bonuses'␀Balls:␀Above Balls␀Below Balls␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêIf you can't see the ball because of all the debris coming down set this option to 'Below Balls'␀Debris:␀By Click␀Auto␀âˆçº'␀␀␀␀If a ball does not damage a brick within ten seconds it is allowed to return to the paddle. If this option is set to 'Auto' it will automatically return and if this option is set to 'By Click' you'll have to press the middle mousebutton or the 'back'-key (default is Backspace).␀Return Balls:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêEnable/disable these quick hints. See the manual for more information about how to use LBreakout2!␀Use Hints:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêAfter you destroyed this percentage of bricks you MAY warp to the next level by pressing 'w'. That is indicated by a small icon at the bottom right-hand side of the screen.#If you set this option to 0 you may instantly warp whereas 100 means you have to destroy all bricks.##Note, that this option does not apply for the levelsets 'Original' and 'LBreakout1'!␀Warp Limit:␀ç∂␀␀␀␀çø␀␀␀␀Network communication is handled by a single UDP socket which will be bound to this port number.␀Local UDP Port:␀ÎêêêêêêêêêêêêêWhile you keep the middle mouse button pressed (or the acceleration key) all balls will go this velocity. (in pixels per second)␀Acc. Ball Speed:␀ç¥&␀␀␀␀çº'␀␀␀␀This is the list of the levelsets found in ~/.lgames/lbreakout2-levels which you may edit. If you choose <CREATE SET> and click on 'Edit Set' below you'll be asked to enter a levelsetname and the new levelset will be saved in a file by this name.␀Set:␀çt&␀Click here to edit the levelset chosen above.##NOTE: To switch to the bonus set you'll have to right-click on the brick set and vice versa!␀Edit Set␀çt&␀çº'␀␀␀␀Click here to delete the chosen levelset (after confirmation).␀Yes␀No␀Theme:␀êêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêêClick here to apply the theme you selected above. Please check the manual at lgames.sf.net for information on how to create a theme.␀Apply␀Cancel␀UâÂÅÏ∏␀␀«Ö†˙ˇˇ‹@␀«Ö§˙ˇˇ&‹@␀«Öà˙ˇˇ.‹@␀«Öå˙ˇˇ2‹@␀«Öê˙ˇˇ6‹@␀«Öî˙ˇˇ=‹@␀«Öx˙ˇˇB‹@␀«Ö|˙ˇˇG‹@␀«ÖÄ˙ˇˇ6‹@␀«ÖÑ˙ˇˇL‹@␀«Öt˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Öp˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Öl˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Öh˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Öd˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Ö`˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Ö\˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«ÖX˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«ÖT˙ˇˇ␀␀␀␀ËòŸˇˇËËˇˇÉÏˇ5#E␀Ë!w␀␀ÉƒÉÏçÖ®˙ˇˇPË;␀␀ÉƒjjzjaçÖ®˙ˇˇPËC␀␀Éƒ«Ö»˙ˇˇ␀␀␀«Ö(˚ˇˇ␀␀␀«Ödˇˇˇ␀␀␀«Öhˇˇˇ␀␀␀«Öxˇˇˇ␀␀␀«Ötˇˇˇ␀␀␀«Öpˇˇˇ␀␀␀«Ölˇˇˇ␀␀␀«ÖÏ˛ˇˇ␀␀␀«Ö˛ˇˇ␀␀␀«Ö¯˛ˇˇ␀␀␀«ÖÙ˛ˇˇ␀␀␀«Öl¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Öh¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Ö@¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Öt¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Ö,¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Öp¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«ÖH¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀«Ö8¸ˇˇ␀␀␀␀ÉÏh≈¿@␀jËÓ8␀Éƒ£¿ E␀jˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hQ‹@␀ËÄ ˇˇÉƒ âÖt˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hV‹@␀ËK ˇˇÉƒ âÖl˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀h_‹@␀Ë ˇˇÉƒ âÖh˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hj‹@␀Ë·…ˇˇÉƒ âÖd˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hs‹@␀Ë¨…ˇˇÉƒ âÖ`˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hÑ‹@␀Ëw…ˇˇÉƒ âÖp˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hä‹@␀ËB…ˇˇÉƒ âÖ\˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hë‹@␀Ë…ˇˇÉƒ âÖX˙ˇˇjˇ5‡ E␀ˇ5‹ E␀ˇ5ÿ E␀ˇ5‘ E␀ˇ5– E␀j␀hú‹@␀Ëÿ»ˇˇÉƒ âÖT˙ˇˇÉÏÉÏˇµh˙ˇˇh¿‹@␀h_‹@␀Ë§¬ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇË1 ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏjh␀›@␀h5›@␀Ë•¬ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇË ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏjj␀hB›@␀Ë¬ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇË‚…ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏhM›@␀Ët¿ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇË¿…ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏˇµd˙ˇˇj␀hj‹@␀Ë	¬ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇËñ…ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏˇµl˙ˇˇj␀hV‹@␀Ëﬂ¡ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇËl…ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏˇµp˙ˇˇj␀hÑ‹@␀Ëµ¡ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇËB…ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏˇµ`˙ˇˇj␀hs‹@␀Ëã¡ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇË…ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏhM›@␀Ë™øˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇËˆ»ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏˇµ\˙ˇˇj␀hä‹@␀Ë?¡ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇËÃ»ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏhM›@␀Ë^øˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇË™»ˇˇÉƒÉÏÉÏjh`›@␀h¢›@␀Ë¡ˇˇÉƒPˇµt˙ˇˇËÅ»ˇˇÉƒÉÏhß›@␀h.‹@␀h®lG␀j␀h™›@␀ËcøˇˇÉƒ âEƒãEƒ«@D
